      <div type="clause" n="65">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 65</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Burhbote. Gyf hwa buruhbote oððe brygcebote oððe fyrdfare forsitte, gebete mid hundtwentigum scill' ðam kyncge on Engle lage, ⁊ on Dena lage swa hit ær stod, oððe geladige hine, (⁊) namige man him XIIII ⁊ begyte XI.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">The repair of fortifications. If anyone neglects the repair of fortifications or of bridges or military service, he shall pay 120 shillings as compensation to the king in districts under English law, and in the Danelaw the amount fixed by existing regulations; or he shall clear himself—[the court] shall nominate 14 compurgators for him and he shall obtain the support of 11 of them.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Gif hwa burhbote oððe brycgbote oððe fyrdfare forsitte, gebete mid CXX scyll' þam cingce on Engla lage, ⁊ on Dena lage swa hit ær stod; oððe geladige hine: namie man him XIIII, ⁊ begyte XI.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
